//? Title: Sparse-grid exploration schedule
//? Lang: en

> Sparse-grid exploration schedule

This fixture gives an exploration algorithm 2,048 actions on a
seven-by-seven grid. Actions move up, down, left or right, with the
current coordinate clipped to the grid boundary. The agent starts in
the upper-left cell and receives a task reward of one on entering the
lower-right cell. An episode resets there or after 64 actions.

Two tabular learners share every transition. The behavior table adds
half the supplied curiosity reward and chooses epsilon-greedy actions
with exploration probability one quarter. The task table sees only the
goal reward and supplies the greedy evaluation policy. Every sixteen
actions, the training callback receives 32 transitions sampled with
replacement from replay. It uses a random stream separate from action
selection. An episode reset callback lets stateful curiosity modules
clear episodic state while retaining their learned parameters.

This example compares task-only training with a constant bonus callback
to illustrate the schedule. A constant bonus rewards visits uniformly.
See [random network distillation|random_network_distillation.mepml]
for a predictor that gives different bonuses to different observations.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/exploration_grid.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

int main() {
  int resets=0,updates=0;
  const auto [control,zero,control_count,control_goals,control_success]=dm::rl::sparse_grid_experiment(43602);
  const auto [path,bonus,count,goals,success]=dm::rl::sparse_grid_experiment(43602,
      [](const auto&) { return .1f; },
      [&](const auto batch) {
        if (batch.size()!=32) throw std::runtime_error("Unexpected replay batch size");
        ++updates;
      },
      [&] { ++resets; });
  if (updates!=128) throw std::runtime_error("Unexpected replay update count");
  const auto accumulate=[](const dm::nn::Tensor& rows) {
    const auto values=rows.to_vector<int>();
    std::set<int> seen{0};
    std::vector<double> coverage{1};
    for (std::size_t i=2;i<values.size();i+=3) {
      seen.insert(values[i]);
      coverage.push_back(seen.size());
    }
    return coverage;
  };
  const auto baseline=accumulate(control), curiosity=accumulate(path);
  if (baseline.back()!=control_count || curiosity.back()!=count) {
    throw std::runtime_error("Coverage differs from the transition trace");
  }
  std::vector<double> steps(baseline.size());
  std::iota(steps.begin(),steps.end(),0.);
  std::print("| Schedule | Visited cells | Training goals | Greedy task success |\n"
             "|:---|---:|---:|:---|\n"
             "| Task only | {} | {} | {} |\n"
             "| Constant bonus | {} | {} | {} |\n\n"
             "The constant-bonus run made {} replay updates and called reset {} times, including initialization.\n",
             control_count,control_goals,control_success,count,goals,success,updates,resets);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  plot.lines(steps,baseline,"Task reward only",{217,96,26})
      .lines(steps,curiosity,"Constant bonus",{37,99,235})
      .title("Sparse-grid coverage over time").x_label("Actions").y_label("Unique cells visited")
      .ylim(0,49).size(820,460).save_svg("build/exploration_grid.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| Schedule | Visited cells | Training goals | Greedy task success |
|:---|---:|---:|:---|
| Task only | 18 | 0 | false |
| Constant bonus | 7 | 0 | false |

The constant-bonus run made 128 replay updates and called reset 33 times, including initialization.
